gptokeyb patch 01 -- immediate ordinary Start/Back while retaining kill chord.

Base: https://github.com/PortsMaster/gptokeyb
commit 5b1284e1502548d476aa38e5979b0a8f48cb7b94.

The upstream kill mode treats both Start and Back/Select as chord prefixes. It
therefore withholds their mapped keys until button release. MGS2 uses both as
ordinary keyboard controls and also sees the physical controller through Wine,
so this was observable as delayed input and a transient unrelated game action.

Add an explicit, default-off option which emits those two mappings on the real
button edge while leaving the same-device Start+Back state and doKillMode()
gate intact. A combined chord may emit the first mapped edge before termination;
that is intentional, bounded by the second edge and irrelevant after the target
is killed. All other ports retain upstream behaviour.

